{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/191516-need-help-with-arcane-homebrew","id":191516,"title":"Need help with Arcane Homebrew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-08T10:35:42-07:00","id":191516,"title":"Need help with Arcane Homebrew","content":"I never really gravitated towards the way lores were presented in Witchfinders. I wrote up two merits that I thought could be used in conjunction with MtAw, but am not sure if they're game breaking or not. Can you guys look and critique?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>New Merit: Student of the Arcane (\u2022\u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> Prerequisites: Must have at least 1 dot in the Occult Skill.<br /> <br /> This merit can be purchased multiple times, with each purchase requiring you to choose one of the ten Awakened Arcana. With the 3 dot version, the character can cast Rank 1 spells from 1 of the Awakened Arcana. With the 4 dot version, the character can cast both Rank 1 and 2 spells from the same Awakened Arcana. And finally, with the 5 dot version, the character can cast spells up to the 3rd rank. Spells learned this way are cast using one Attribute, determined upon purchase, and the Occult Skill. Each casting requires either an appropriate sacrament, or Source.<br /> <br /> <b><i>New Merit: Arcane Ritual (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> Prerequisites: Must have at least 4 dots in Occult Skill.<br /> <br /> This merit can be purchased multiple times, each representing a single spell of rank 4 or 5, depending on version purchased. Even if said-spell would normally be instantaneous, the ritual-version is always extended, and requires a number of sacraments equal to normal Mana cost +1, each of which being appropriate to the spell's nature. The dice pool for the ritual is determined on purchase, comprised of one Attribute, and the Occult Skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 07-08-2014, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T14:18:24-07:00","id":195762,"title":"","content":"So are you using these merits to emulate Dread Powers? How would you handle Paradox?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T14:28:20-07:00","id":195768,"title":"","content":"Well, specifically, they're meant to be an alternative for mortal and Hunter PCs alike if people want to use stuff from the mage books. Regarding paradox, I haven't figured out how best to handle it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T03:42:25-07:00","id":196171,"title":"","content":"Well if you want to limit them in another way than paradox you can have the spellcasting weaken the user through damage: bashing, lethal, or maybe even agg if you want some spells to be costly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T07:35:49-07:00","id":196270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/191516-need-help-with-arcane-homebrew?p=196171#post196171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well if you want to limit them in another way than paradox you can have the spellcasting weaken the user through damage: bashing, lethal, or maybe even agg if you want some spells to be costly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... well, what if covert spells above rank 1 cause bashing damage, while vulgar caused lethal? Any with a listed mana cost upgrades the damage by one tier, so bashing becomes lethal, lethal becomes agg, etc. Even with sacraments, you can only downgrade the damage to the lowest possible tier. In doing so, however, you converts the original damage to double. So 1 lethal becomes 2 bashing, while 1 agg becomes 2 lethal or 4 bashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T07:02:20-07:00","id":196751,"title":"","content":"Alright, made some alterations to the merits. Tell me what you guys think. I may have reserves about certain loopholes, like a spellcaster getting a healing spell to fix drain damage. Also not sure how to figure alternate splats into it. If these merits exist, what would stop a vampire or changeling from learning them? Should I fix that, or leave it be?<br /> <br /> <b><i>Student of the Arcane (\u2022\u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> Prerequisites: Must have at least 1 dot in the Occult Skill.<br /> <br /> This merit can be purchased multiple times, with each purchase requiring you to choose one of the ten Awakened Arcana. With the 3 dot version, the character can cast Rank 1 spells from 1 of the Awakened Arcana. With the 4 dot version, the character can cast both Rank 1 and 2 spells from the same Awakened Arcana. And finally, with the 5 dot version, the character can cast spells up to the 3rd rank. Spells learned this way are cast using one Attribute, determined upon purchase, and the Occult Skill. Each casting requires either an appropriate sacrament, or Source.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> any and all covert spells above rank 1 of an arcanum cause 1 bashing damage to cast. Vulgar spells cause 1 lethal. If a mana cost is listed with the spell, it requires spending Willpower points equal to said-mana cost. Magical implements can be used to downgrade damage, but never nullify it entirely. When damage is downgraded, it becomes double its original number for the new tier, eg. 1 lethal becomes 2 bashing.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Arcane Ritual (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> Prerequisites: Must have at least 4 dots in the Occult Skill.<br /> <br /> This merit can be purchased multiple times, each representing a single spell of rank 4 or 5, depending on version purchased. Even if said-spell would normally be instantaneous, the ritual-version is always extended, and requires a number of sacraments equal to normal Mana cost +1, each of which being appropriate to the spell's nature. The dice pool for the ritual is determined on purchase, comprised of one Attribute, and the Occult Skill. More than one person can assist in casting the ritual, but one of them must have the prerequisites to cast the spell. This individual, the rite master, rolls the dice pool as well as suffers whatever any damage incurred by the drawback (see below). Anyone aiding in the ritual adds +1 to the dicepool (or +2 if they're trained in the Occult skill). If willing, they may take damage in the rite master's place, dividing it among themselves.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Covert spells made into rituals cause 2 bashing damage to cast. Vulgar spells cause 2 lethal. If a mana cost is listed, the rite master must sacrifice an equal number of Willpower points. Magical implements can downgrade the damage to the next tier, at the price of doubling it--eg. 2 lethal become 4 bashing. Damage cannot be nullified in this fashion. If an appropriate sacrament cannot be found, the rite master may alternatively deal 1 aggravated damage to themselves, in addition to whatever damage the ritual would normally cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T00:30:14-07:00","id":199738,"title":"","content":"Well, if you consider supernaturals expanding their powers as a bad thing, you can make these merits supernatural merits, so only muggles and a few splats that have access to supernatural merits need apply.<br /> <br /> Or you might consider making student of the arcane a supernatural merit and leaving arcane ritual open to anyone. Ritual magic often has the assumption that the power is in the ritual, so it doesn't matter who casts them, examples of that idea in nwod include exorcisms, mysteries cast as rituals in witchfinders, the ritual magic for everyone option in the mage chroniclers guide, and occultism in antagonists. So if you do that, student of the arcane is an inherent gift for magic that nevertheless doesn't make the person a mage, but arcane ritual represents knowing a specific ritual that anyone can do. If you do that you might want to open up the merit for rituals to emulate rotes from level 1 on up instead of saving it for the higher levels of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T05:07:56-07:00","id":199898,"title":"","content":"Clever. Very very clever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My only fear is that the magic of those rituals somehow ruins a splat--eg: a vampire learning life magic when blood sorcery is meant to be somewhat tainted and incapable of truly creating life, simply replicating or imitating (as stated in the Blood Sorcery supplement). Then again, not everyone has access to that book, or even cares. Guess it could still work...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}